HELDHEADER|step=09-federation-kernel-2026-05|date=2026-10-18 (token rows added 2026-10-19)|rule=OWNER-RULES HOLD (tokens; files whose content holds a real credential) + OWNER-RULES 7.j/7.m + the 05-13 staging README's own rule ("Keep runtime data, screenshots, bus receipts, and private topology out of Git")|note=Nothing in these rows is vendored. Four federation genesis files are held because they carry tokens (the first four rows). W18-WAVE-SYNTHESIS-ACER-2026-05-12.md carries the full 36-character BEAST bearer UUID (a2548ed8-...), the same live token as line 40 of gates/hookwall-v2.js (Asolaria mirror blob 76e19530, held by step 6), and the usb_raw_io auth token. substrate-conflict-matrix.json, SUBSTRATE_CONFLICT_MATRIX.md and kernel/docs/DRIVER_MODEL.md carry only the usb_raw_io auth token literal; they are held under the token rule until the owner decides whether to release them. The first scan of 2026-10-18 missed all four: it matched "Bearer" case-sensitively and "token": only, so it did not see the lowercase "bearer" or "auth_token":. Seven candidate rows of the federation genesis (6 distinct PNG blobs, one at two paths) are ACER desktop screen captures, held as runtime captures that may show private windows; their .behcs-1024.json receipts carry no image bytes and are vendored. One row records the HyperBEHCS vote_quorum daemon, held by rule 7.j (restated in 7.m), which was never committed to any public repo. The 2026-10-19 rescan of the 176 files still vendored was case-insensitive (gh_/ghp_/github_pat_/sk-/AIza/hf_/xox/AKIA/eyJ prefixes, BEGIN ... KEY, ssh-rsa/ssh-ed25519, bearer, authorization, token/auth_token/secret/password/api_key assignments with a literal value, UUIDs, emails, phone numbers, whatsapp) and found no credential: every sk- hit ends an ordinary word (spacedesk-, risk-, disk-, task-); the 5 bearer hits are the BearerMissing error variant in both versions of bus_and_kick/mod.rs and one plan line preferring bearer-token routes; the only UUID is a Claude session id cited twice in super-dashboard-server.mjs; the private-key hits are code comments with no key bytes; the only email is the owner's own Gmail (staging tools/Start-Asolaria.ps1, released under 7.m); the rest are LAN addresses (192.168.1.x, 192.168.100.x, 172.26.128.1), local paths and the five authorized operators' names (rule 5).|json=0
